+## Environment Variables Reference
 
-After the LLM returns a JSON insight, `validate_llm_output()` enforces the report schema:
+Settings are read from the process environment, then `cji_agent/.env` (never read when `CJI_ENV=test`).
+`.env.example` documents every key. `python -m settings check --role <role>` prints the resolved values with secrets
+redacted and exits 2 on a configuration error (roles: `cli`, `dashboard`, `collector`, `launcher`, `mcp:<service>`).
 
-| Field | Validation | Auto-correction |
+| Variable | Default | Description |
 |---|---|---|
-| `title` | Non-empty string, ≤ 8 words | Truncated or defaulted to `"Friction detected at <step>"` |
-| `category` | Must be in `{UX, data, system, process, unknown}` | Replaced with `"unknown"` |
-| `fix_effort` | Must be in `{low, medium, high}` | Replaced with `"medium"` |
-| `root_cause` | Non-empty string | Replaced with `"Root cause details were not provided."` |
-| `suggested_fix` | Non-empty string | Replaced with `"Review metrics manually."` |
-| `evidence` | Must be a list | Replaced with `[]` |
-| *(Not a dict)* | Entire response is malformed | `_fallback()` returns a safe default insight |
